0 !ACHILLES {"id":"ACH-Z04-S03","name":"Zone IV · Scene 3: Labors of the Field — The Golden Vineyard & Linus Song","zone":"Z04","lines":"18.561–572","greek":"Ἐν δ᾽ ἐτίθει σταφυλῇσι μέγα βρίθουσαν ἀλωὴν καλὴν χρυσείην· μέλανες δ᾽ ἀνὰ βότρυες ἦσαν, ἑστήκει δὲ κάμαξι διαμπερὲς ἀργυρέῃσιν. ἀμφὶ δὲ κυανέην κάπετον, περὶ δ᾽ ἕρκος ἔλασσε κασσιτέροιο· μία δ᾽ οἴη ἀταρπὸς ἐπ᾽ αὐτὴν... τοῖσιν δ᾽ ἐν μέσσοισι πάϊς φόρμιγγι λιγείῃ ἱμερόεν κιθάριζε, λίνον δ᾽ ὑπὸ καλὸν ἄειδε λεπταλέῃ φωνῇ· τοὶ δὲ ῥήσσοντες ἁμαρτῇ μολπῇ τ᾽ ἰυγμῷ τε ποσὶ σκαίροντες ἕποντο.","buckley":"On it also he placed a vineyard heavily laden with grapes, beautiful, golden; but the clusters throughout were black; and it was supported throughout by silver poles. Around it he drew a dark-blue trench, and around a hedge of tin; and there was but one path to it, by which the gatherers went, when they collected the vintage. Young virgins and youths, of tender minds, carried the sweet fruit in woven baskets. In the midst of them a boy played pleasantly on a shrill lyre, and sung the beautiful Linus song with a slender voice; while they, beating the ground in accompaniment, with singing and shouting, followed, hopping with their feet.","worldModel":{"vision":"Five-metal polyphony in a single zone: golden vines (297), black clusters (0/22), silver poles (179), dark-blue kyanos trench (272/33), and tin fence (71) with a single path.","memory":"Topological constraint (μία δ᾽ οἴη ἀταρπὸς — one single path in and out) channeling the rhythmic procession of basket-bearers.","controller":"The boy’s shrill phorminx and slender Linus song synchronizing the stamping feet of the youths and maidens."}}

